The first set of queries improved the best observed output for **five of the eight functions**. Function 5 showed a particularly substantial improvement, while Functions 1 and 6 did not improve despite the exploratory selections. This reinforced the need to review their surrogate models rather than rely on the same approach indefinitely.

## Data Organisation and Next Steps

The original Week 1 observations are stored as `initial_inputs.npy` and `initial_outputs.npy` in the [`Data`](../Data/) directory, organised by function. The notebook that loads these files and generates the proposed points is [`Week_01.ipynb`](../Python_Files/Week_01.ipynb).

From **Week 2 onwards**, the project uses per-function CSV files to record the accumulated observations available at the start of each week. Each new returned result is incorporated into the next week's dataset so that subsequent models can be fitted using the complete observation history. This also makes it easier to inspect how the data and optimisation strategy developed over time.

In Week 2, I will update the models with the returned outputs, investigate the poor generalisation observed in Functions 1 and 6, and continue balancing local refinement with exploration in the remaining functions.

